---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Skills and plugins"
  description="Discover Agent Skills and experimental Agent Plugins MCP in Veasel Code."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / SKILLS</p>
    <h1>
      Skills you already
      <br />
      <em>keep nearby.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel discovers standalone <code>SKILL.md</code> folders from project and
      user roots used by other agents, plus experimental Agent Plugin packages.
      Instructions are reference context — scripts are never auto-executed.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Standalone skill discovery</h2>
      <p>Scanned roots include (project + matching home directories):</p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <code>.agents/skills</code>, <code>.claude/skills</code>,{" "}
          <code>.codex/skills</code>, <code>.cursor/skills</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>.opencode/skills</code>, <code>.gemini/skills</code>,{" "}
          <code>.pi/skills</code>, <code>.qwen/skills</code>,{" "}
          <code>.github/skills</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          Extra directories via <code>VEASEL_SKILLS_DIRS</code>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <pre><code>/skills              # list discovered skills
/skills auth         # filter
/skill on my-skill   # enable for this session
/skill off my-skill

# Headless (metadata only — never prints instruction bodies)
veasel skills list
veasel skills list --directory /path/to/project --json</code></pre>
      <p>
        HTTP: <code>GET /v1/skills</code> (<code>skills.discovery</code>).
        Capability discovery also lists synthetic plugin catalog entries when
        skills exist without <code>plugin.json</code>. Skill scripts are never
        auto-executed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Plugin component toggles</h2>
      <p>
        Disable individual skill or MCP components from a linked Agent Plugin
        without removing the package link. Overrides live in{" "}
        <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/plugin-components.json</code> (
        <code>plugins.components</code>):
      </p>
      <pre><code>veasel plugins components list
veasel plugins components disable demo mcp local
veasel plugins components enable demo skill review</code></pre>
      <p>
        Disabled skills cannot be session-activated; disabled MCP servers cannot
        be trusted. HTTP: <code>GET/PATCH /v1/plugins/components</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Agent Plugins (experimental)</h2>
      <p>
        Packages are discovered from <code>$VEASEL_PLUGIN_DIR</code> or{" "}
        <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/plugins</code>. Link a local package directory
        with <code>/plugin add &lt;path&gt;</code> (or{" "}
        <code>/v1/plugins/links</code>) — Veasel does not fetch remote packages.
        Support covers Skills plus trusted stdio / Streamable HTTP MCP —{" "}
        <strong>not full Agent Plugins v1.0.0 conformance</strong>. Track the
        ledger:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/compatibility/agent-plugins.md">
          docs/compatibility/agent-plugins.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Prefer standalone configured MCP when you only need a server: see the{" "}
          <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a> (
          <code>/mcp add [user|project]</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Plugin MCP servers need per-session trust (
          <code>/mcp trust &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;server&gt;</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Every model-requested MCP tool call requires separate inspection and
          one-time approval.
        </li>
        <li>
          Trusted stdio MCP processes inherit the server user and are not OS
          sandboxed. Streamable HTTP refuses redirects and validates TLS.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Untrusted instructions.</strong> Skill bodies and MCP results may
      be sent to your configured provider once enabled or approved. Treat them
      like any other untrusted tool output.
    </aside>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        MCP servers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/plugins/`}>
        Compatibility notes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>
        Security model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
